A new version of JOE is out (get by anonymous ftp from ftp.std.com, file:
src/editors/joe1.0.12.tar.Z).  This version includes a number of fixes and
improvements from version 1.0.8:

	- ^T. and ^T- are macros which call ispell to check a word or
	  a block or file

	- ESC w and ESC z do WordStar-style single line scrolling.  You can
	  remap these to ^W and ^Z if you really want JOE to look like
	  wordstar.

	- A bug where only 2 bytes would be saved to file when the '-force'
	  option is on is fixed.

	- A bug which prevented JOE from running on AT&T 3B2s is fixed.  I
          think this bug may solve some random crash problems people are
	  reporting.

	- The messages for wordwrap and autoindent mode are fixed

	- JOE now works on DEC Alphas

