X Inside Inc has a high performance X Server available for Linux.
The server is a replacement for the XFree86 Server (i.e. install 
XFree86 server, fonts, clients and libs and then install 
Accelerated-X Server).  The server supports modern high performance 
graphics accelerator chipsets, such as the Matrox MGA series, ATI 
Mach 64, S3 964, Number 9 I-128, Cirrus GD5434, etc.

We're not keen on benchmarks, because unless they are independently
conducted and certified (and even then...) they can be spoofed.  On
an untuned Pentium/60 with a Matrox MGA, PCI board, we can measure
more than 350,000 xStones, about 6.5 Xmarks.  The server is visibly
faster than anything else we, or our existing customers, have seen.  
The I-128 should get better than 450,000 xStones on the same H/W and
OS, when it is in production.

Some of the core technology has been licensed by SunSoft for Solaris
2.4.  ICL, BSDI, ELSA are OEM's for non-Linux versions.  The product
is OS Neutral; one compilation of the driver works on all supported
OS's, reducing our time to market and to resolve problems.

The server supports up to 8 screens in a multihead display (most
easily implemented with ColorGraphic Dual Lightning or Twin Turbo
boards); Mouse or Tablet; up to 1600x1200 virtual desktop on suitable
H/W; dynamically loaded extensions include all popular font formats.

We do not currently provide PEX, XIE or the various *GL flavors.  If
someone needs them, we can provide them, but we only know of student
projects... and if you're a student doing that kind of graphics, you
probably port your own X, anyway :-)  VAR and quantity end user 
interest in these extensions is welcomed.

