Announcing CHAT 0.2 alpha
-------------------------

I've uploaded CHAT 0.2, a multiuser chat utility, to 
ftp.gwdg.de and sunsite.unc.edu.

CHAT can be installed by any user on a system (not only root).
Users connect to it via telnet to a specific port and talk
together. Any number of CHAT servers can be installed on a
system simultaneously to support independent discussions on
various topics.

There is also a private conversation mode, in which two users
can talk together without being observed by the other CHAT users.

This version of CHAT is an alpha, so please send observations and
suggestions to me. Further features will be added soon. If you do
something interesting with CHAT, please tell me about it.

CHAT is distributed according to the GNU GPL.

Here is the (old-style) lsm entry. I append the README to the
program after the lsm entry so that you can evaluate if the
program does what you need.

-------------------------------------------------------------
Begin2 
Title        = Chat - a multiuser chat utility via telnet
Version      = 0.2
Desc1        = Multiple users connect via telnet to chat and can
Desc2        = talk together. Configured for up to 15 users but
Desc3        = this limit can be changed by recompilation.
Desc4        = Simple to use, private conversation mode supported.
Desc5	     = Installable by user, no root access needed.
Author       = Andreas Matthias, Rolf Krahl
