Just as I released userfs 0.8, Linus decided to use long longs in
the kernel, which breaks the genser part of userfs.

Here's a patch which adds long long support to genser.  Apply
this patch in the genser directory and rebuild userfs.

This patch will also be available in:

   tsx-11.mit.edu: pub/linux/ALPHA/userfs/userfs-0.8-0.8.1.diff.gz
   sunsite.unc.edu: pub/Linux/ALPHA/userfs/userfs-0.8-0.8.1.diff.gz

	J


