symlinks v0.4 has been uploaded to tsx-11.mit.edu,
and is now available as:

	/pub/linux/sources/usr.bin/symlinks-0.4.tar.gz

symlinks is a utility which scans a directory structure for symbolic
links and reports on what it finds, classifying the links as relative,
absolute, other_fs, or dangling.  It can also optionally convert all
applicable absolute links to relative links within a filesystem,
for consistent access when not mounted at the usual mount point
(ie. when booting from floppy).

This utility is highly recommended for anyone preparing a linux distribution
or CD-ROM.  It has uncovered errors in every distribution I've tried it on
thus far..

