The latest release of my PCMCIA Card Services package is available on
cb-iris.stanford.edu in /pub/pcmcia/pcmcia-cs-1.7.tgz.

This version includes patches for a 1.1.38 kernel, but I don't think
there is anything in 1.1.39 that would cause problems.

Both Intel i82365sl (or clone) and Databook TCIC/2 PCMCIA controllers
are supported.  Hot swapping of PCMCIA cards is fully supported.  Card
configuration is completely automatic.  And all the PCMCIA code is
packaged in loadable modules.  Drivers for specific cards are loaded
on demand.

This package is still somewhat experimental -- don't install it unless
you will be willing to help me work out any problems you might find.

The following cards are known to work:

Ethernet:
	D-Link DE-650
	Linksys E-Card
	IC-Card
	3Com 3c589

Modems:
	AT&T KeepInTouch Card
	AST 14.4/14.4 FAX modem
	IBM High-speed Fax/Modem
	Intel 14.4/14.4 Faxmodem
	Megahertz XJ1440
	US Robotics Worldport 14400

-- David Hinds
